{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPgNLqNiCjJQsTSD5TPu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #385 as `done`: the triage engineer plans it and the engineer worker implements it. The decision is in `.ard/385/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Why it can start now:** the issue depends on part 1 (#384), and part 1 has landed on main as commit e2428bd (#398). So the status is `done`, not `blocked`.\n- **Why only the engineer:** the only roles in the repo are the engineer (triage and worker), the lead and the `eng-review` reviewer. There is no architect role, though this change would normally get one because it touches the label lifecycle and the proposal. `eng-review` has no `when:` rule in `.ard/config.yaml`, so it runs on every pull request and doesn't need a `review:` entry.\n- **Open issues I listed for maintainers:**\n  - With no architect role, the triage engineer should follow the design in the parent issue, #277.\n  - Updating the live prompts under `.ard/` is out of scope; those files are protected, and a human pull request will change them later. The issue only changes the starter copies in `internal/roles/`.\n  - The bounce must stay switched off in `servecmd` until part 3 lands, so reviewers should check that live behaviour doesn't change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":730,"cache_read_input_tokens":12285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":730},"output_tokens":404,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cb0c198-da76-4562-9cd9-f218db6c9d82","uuid":"c8058cc2-8ffd-4420-bef8-0fa1ec759f8e","timestamp":"2026-11-25T12:53:44.462Z","request_id":"req_011ChPgNLgx5Duute2vaUUQs"}
